s://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=3\nSnippet: Intervals.icu uses OAuth2 for authentication to the API. OAuth allows external applications to request authorization to access an ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-04-01\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609\nSnippet: Intervals.icu now has a public API for other applications. using OAuth. calendar events. Requires parameters oldest and newest in yyyy-MM-dd ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2024-11-20\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\nSnippet: This tells you everything you need to know to get completed activities into and out of Intervals.icu, to download planned workouts and to read ...\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_aTvPPUVyfpj9sFWE7HgD25WY","content":"Title: [BUG] MCP OAuth tokens without expires_in and refresh_token silently expires\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-02-17\nURL: https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/26281\nSnippet: What's Wrong? When an MCP server's OAuth token exchange endpoint `/oauth/token` returns only an `access_token` without `expires_in` or `refresh_token` (e.g. GitHub OAuth tokens), Claude Code silently expires the credential after some time (more than 30 minutes but less than 24 hours) and requires re-authentication. After the token expires, Claude Code attempts the MCP `initialize` request without the Authorization header, which fails. The user must then manually re-authenticate via `/mcp`. The t\n\n---\n\nTitle: Refresh_token_expires_in not getting from google OAuth token api by passing ServerAuthCode.\nSite: Github\nDate: 2025-12-02\nURL: https://github.com/google/GoogleSignIn-iOS/issues/565\nSnippet: Describe the bug I am getting a serverAuthCode which doesn't gives Refresh_token_expires_in from google Oauth token api call when user not checkmarked the ongoing access for google account. To Reproduce Steps to reproduce the behavior: 1. Call GIDSignIn.sharedInstance.signIn(withPresenting: rootViewController, hint: email, additionalScopes: scopes) 2. User get prompted for google sign inand then scopes list will be shown to the user. 3. User will not select Ongoing access and select all required\n\n---\n\nTitle: banshu-ai 1.1.0\nSite: Docs.rs\nDate: 2026-10-27\nURL: https://docs.rs/crate/banshu-ai/latest/source/src/kimi.rs\nSnippet: ... api/oauth/token` for both the device-code poll //! and the refresh-token ... expires_in: Option, interval: Option ... response .json::() ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth server token (/oauth/token/) | REST API Solution Guide\nSite: Fortinet Documentation\nURL: https://docs.fortinet.com/document/fortiauthenticator/8.0.1/rest-api-solution-guide/498666/oauth-server-token-oauth-token\nSnippet: OAuth server token (/oauth/token/) Response codes ``` Get token (Password-based) curl -k -v -X POST https://[FAC_IP]/api/v1/oauth/token/ -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{ \"username\": \"luser1\", \"password\": \"12345678\", \"client_id\": \"client_id\", \"client_secret\": \"client_secret\", -> in case of confidential \"grant_type\": \"password\" }' Response: { \"access_token\": \"shrWNdu1xJRUgpcUi2bhYRX1Sl8pXe\", \"expires_in\": 0, \"message\": \"successfully authenticated\", \"refresh_token\": \"tU85BMdOoV3pktSSiLaABJ\n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth refresh token grant type and OAuth access and refresh token expiration\nSite: The place for Zendesk users to come together and share\nDate: 2025-04-30\nURL: https://community.zendesk.com/ideas/oauth-refresh-token-grant-type-and-oauth-access-and-refresh-token-expiration-5637/index3.html\nSnippet: Hi folks! I'm getting the same error as Phil and cannot figure out a way to solve it. I'm trying to introduce refresh token usage into my Zendesk OAuth workflow, but I'm encountering an \"invalid_grant\" error. I'm able to retrieve the token and use it, but not able to utilize refresh token. I'm using this doc page as a reference: https://developer.zendesk.com/api-reference/ticketing/oauth/grant_type_tokens/#create-token-for-grant-type In my authorization call, I'm passing both `expires_in` and `r\n\n---\n\nTitle: Not receiving refresh token at \"/oauth/token\" endpoint - Auth0 Community\nSite: Auth0 Community\nDate: 2024-10-01\nURL: https://community.auth0.com/t/not-receiving-refresh-token-at-oauth-token-endpoint/148340\nSnippet: olaskole4405's profile I am currently using the Universal login flow along with the authorization code flow to login a user. After authorizing the user via the universal login page, I receive the authorization code which I then send to my API. My API then calls the oauth/token endpoint to exchange the authorization code for a access token and a refresh token. The response contains the access token only, along with the expires_in and token type fields, but the refresh token is missing. I included\n\n---\n\nTitle: Oracle API Gateway OAuth User Guide\nSite: oracle.com\nDate: 2015-07-27\nURL: https://docs.oracle.com/cd/E65459_01/user.1112/E65456_01.pdf\nSnippet: The OAuth 2.0 Access Token using JWT filter enables an OAuth client to request an access token ... https://127.0.0.1:8089/api/oauth/token). The ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Google OAuth Refresh Token Expires After 1 Hour (PHP Google Ads API with Laravel)\nSite: Stack Overflow\nDate: 2024-04-19\nURL: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/78353257/google-oauth-refresh-token-expires-after-1-hour-php-google-ads-api-with-laravel\nSnippet: My Google OAuth refresh token expires after one hour, even though both my OAuth and Google Ads API applications are verified and approved. - Both OAuth and Google Ads API apps are verified and approved. - Created a new client_credentials.json file after approval. - Using the provided Laravel example for the PHP Google Ads API. - Added the developer token with basic access and populated clientId and clientSecret in the google_ads_php.ini file. For the refresh token i used command ~/go/bin/oauth2l\n\n---\n\nTitle: openclaw_oauth_sync/docs/HOW-TOKEN-REFRESH-WORKS.md at main\nSite: git.eeqj.de\nDate: 2026-03-01\nURL: https://git.eeqj.de/ROOH/openclaw_oauth_sync/src/branch/main/docs/HOW-TOKEN-REFRESH-WORKS.md\nSnippet: Anthropic OAuth Token Lifecycle Claude Max subscriptions use OAuth tokens for API authentication. - Access token ( ``): Used for API requests, expires in ~8 hours - Refresh token ( ``): Used to get new access tokens, long-lived - Token endpoint: `POST https://console.anthropic.com/v1/oauth/token` - Client ID: `9d1c250a-e61b-44d9-88ed-5944d1962f5e` (Claude Code public OAuth client) How Claude Code CLI Refreshes Tokens Claude Code CLI has built-in token refresh. Before each API request: 1. Checks \n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth Token Refresh Issues\nSite: twig.so\nDate: 2026-01-26\nURL: https://www.twig.so/dev/rag-scenarios-and-solutions/data-integration/oauth-refresh\nSnippet: Deep Technical Analysis OAuth 2.0 Token Lifecycle OAuth uses two tokens with different lifespans: Access Token (short-lived): ``` Lifespan: 1-2 hours (varies by provider) Purpose: Make API requests When expired: API returns 401 Example: Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGc... ← access token ``` Refresh Token (long-lived): ``` Lifespan: Days to months (or indefinite) Purpose: Obtain new access token When expired: Must re-authorize Flow: 1. Access token expires 2. Use refresh token to get new access toke\n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth and OpenID Connect | Chief Tools | Chief Tools Documentation\nSite: chief.tools\nURL: https://docs.chief.tools/developers/discovery\nSnippet: Refresh access. When the access token expires, exchange the refresh token at the discovered token endpoint: Code. POST /api/oauth/token HTTP/1.1 Host: account ...\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
