{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_PqfjRhh3NcbHhqOwOfDObk3S","content":"Title: inspectIntervalsPermissions 回報的是發證當下的紀錄，不是 provider 現在認不認\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-08-18\nURL: https://github.com/atomchung/long-run-hybrid-coach/issues/162\nSnippet: Closed — verified against the live account after promotion, 2026-08-18 The delivery itself converged on 2026-08-18 07:22 UTC: the same eight sessions returned `intervals_accepted` after the athlete reconnected. What stayed open was the reason that took a day to find, and it is fixed in #173. The scope question is settled, and the answer is no. intervals.icu publishes six scopes — ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, CHATS, LIBRARY, SETTINGS — with one modifier rule: \"For each scope specify READ or WRIT\n\n---\n\nTitle: kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\nSite: Github\nDate: 2024-01-01\nURL: https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\nSnippet: Manage calendar events, workouts, plans, downloads. Available OAuth scopes: ACTIVITY:READ , ACTIVITY:WRITE WELLNESS:READ , WELLNESS:WRITE CALENDAR:READ , ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth 2.0 Scope Aggregation for Multi-Step AI Agent Workflows\nSite: IETF Datatracker\nDate: 2026-02-10\nURL: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-jia-oauth-scope-aggregation-00\nSnippet: Appendix A. Example of a Resource List This appendix is non-normative. Figure 5 shows an example resource list for a calendar server. In this example, both resources belong to the same authorization domain. For a workflow that accesses both resources, the AI agent can obtain an access token via OAuth 2.0 with the aggregated scope set [\"calendar.read\", \"calendar.write\"]. If the authorization domain defines that \"calendar.write\" subsumes \"calendar.read\", the requested scope set can be further redu\n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth Scopes | Intercom and Fin Developer Platform\nSite: Developer Hub\nURL: https://developers.intercom.com/docs/build-an-integration/learn-more/authentication/oauth-scopes\nSnippet: When you configure OAuth you will need to define the OAuth scopes, and these will be reviewed when you submit your app for approval.\n\n---\n\nTitle: I cannot find scope calendar:read and calendar:admin in the list of zoom scopes for OAuth App - API and Webhooks - Zoom Developer Forum\nSite: Zoom Developer Forum\nDate: 2024-06-04\nURL: https://devforum.zoom.us/t/i-cannot-find-scope-calendar-read-and-calendar-admin-in-the-list-of-zoom-scopes-for-oauth-app/111305\nSnippet: I selected all the available scopes under “Calendar”, and still running into issues. Where and how can I find these two scopes and add them to ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: ueberauth_intervals_icu on Hex\nSite: Libraries.io\nDate: 2026-08-13\nURL: https://libraries.io/hex/ueberauth_intervals_icu\nSnippet: Scopes Permalink: Scopes intervals.icu joins scopes with commas, not the spaces used by most OAuth 2.0 providers: ``` providers: [ intervals_icu: {Ueberauth.Strategy.IntervalsIcu, [default_scope: \"ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE\"]} ] ``` Each scope takes a `:READ` or `:WRITE` suffix: |Scope|Covers| |-|-| |`ACTIVITY`|Activities, intervals, streams| |`WELLNESS`|Wellness records: weight, HRV, resting HR, sleep| |`CALENDAR`|Planned workouts and calendar events| |`CHATS`|Messages| |`LIBRARY`|Workout and\n\n---\n\nTitle: Setting Up Credentials | MCPBundles Docs\nSite: MCP Bundles\nURL: https://www.mcpbundles.com/docs/how-to/setting-up-credentials\nSnippet: Adding OAuth Credentials OAuth is the most secure authentication method. The credential panel stays open throughout the entire process! How OAuth Works (New Context-Aware Flow) 1. Credential panel opens on the right side 2. (Optional) Enter a credential name (e.g., \"Work GitHub\", \"Production Slack\") 3. Click \"Connect with [Provider]\" button 4. OAuth window opens → Log in to provider 5. Review permissions → See what access is requested 6. Click \"Allow\" → Authorize MCPBundles 7. OAuth window close\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu OAuth support - Announcements\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2021-01-30\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\nSnippet: Scopes are as follows: ACTIVITY: Completed rides, runs etc. CALENDAR: Planned workouts. For each scope specify READ or WRITE … separate ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu OAuth support - Page 3\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2021-01-30\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=3\nSnippet: Intervals.icu uses OAuth2 for authentication to the API. These are the scopes: ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, LIBRARY, SETTINGS You need ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Feishu Cli Auth (Grade A) - Claude Skill\nSite: Claude Skill\nDate: 2026-11-06\nURL: https://www.skillsdirectory.com/skills/leoyeai-feishu-cli-auth\nSnippet: Security analysis ``` --- name: feishu-cli-auth description: >- 飞书 OAuth 认证和 User Access Token 管理。两步式非交互登录（AI Agent 专用）、 Token 状态检查、scope 配置、自动刷新机制、搜索功能的 Token 依赖关系。 当用户请求\"登录飞书\"、\"获取 Token\"、\"OAuth 授权\"、\"auth login\"、\"认证\"、 \"搜索需要什么权限\"、\"Token 过期了\"、\"刷新 Token\"时使用。 当遇到权限错误（如 99991679 Unauthorized）、Token 过期、state 不匹配等问题时也应使用此技能。 也适用于：搜索命令报权限错误、Token 相关的排错、需要判断当前授权状态的场景。 当其他飞书技能（toolkit/msg/read 等）遇到 User Access Token 相关问题时，也应参\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2024-11-20\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\nSnippet: This tells you everything you need to know to get completed activities into and out of Intervals.icu, to download planned workouts and to read ...\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
