{"role":"assistant","content":"Now `auth_init` — add `response_type=code` and return the authorize URL as JSON so the SPA can fetch it with the Bearer header:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_W4RKlPCAOC3JWM0Ln3EPwniX","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"new_string\":\"    # Step 1: build the authorize URL for the SPA to navigate to. Returns JSON\\n    # because the caller must authenticate with the Bearer header, which a\\n    # plain link navigation would not send.\\n    def auth_init(self):\\n        user = self.require_user()\\n        if not user:\\n            return\\n        params = {\\\"response_type\\\": \\\"code\\\", \\\"client_id\\\": config.CLIENT_ID,\\n                  \\\"redirect_uri\\\": config.REDIRECT_URI, \\\"scope\\\": config.SCOPES,\\n                  \\\"state\\\": sign_state(user[\\\"id\\\"])}\\n        url = AUTHORIZE_URL + \\\"?\\\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\\\":,\\\")\\n        self.send_json(200, {\\\"url\\\": url})\",\"old_string\":\"    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\\n    def auth_init(self):\\n        user = self.require_user()\\n        if not user:\\n            return\\n        params = {\\\"client_id\\\": config.CLIENT_ID, \\\"redirect_uri\\\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\\n                  \\\"scope\\\": config.SCOPES, \\\"state\\\": sign_state(user[\\\"id\\\"])}\\n        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \\\"?\\\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\\\":,\\\"))\",\"path\":\"server.py\"}"}}]}
